15 passed. Here's a summary of the 10 bugs fixed across 3 modules:

**`src/auth.py`** (3 fixes)
- `has_permission`: was doing case-sensitive `required in user_roles`; now lowercases both sides before comparing
- `is_admin_or_owner`: was `admin AND owner_id == user_id` (needed `or`); also fixed the permission check to use the corrected `has_permission`

**`src/inventory.py`** (4 fixes)
- `__init__`: mutable `{}` default was shared across all instances; changed to `None` and copied
- `add`: was overwriting `_stock[sku] = qty`; now accumulates with `+`
- `reserve`: was `qty >= available` (raises when qty equals available); changed to `qty > available`
- `release`: was allowing negative results; now raises `ValueError` when `qty > current`

**`src/text_utils.py`** (3 fixes)
- `slugify`: wasn't lowercasing output; added `.lower()` on the input loop
- `slugify`: single `.replace("--", "-")` only collapses one occurrence; wrapped in a `while` loop to collapse all runs
- `truncate`: was slicing at `[:max_len]` then appending suffix, making output `max_len + len(suffix)`; now slices at `[:max_len - len(suffix)]`
